hello everyone happy holidays the  mindful Club cookbook is finally here  and I feel like a little kid on  Christmas morning because I am so  excited to have my copy in my hands this  book is a compilation of all of my  favorite and best recipes we've got  breakfast we've got soup salads and  sides main dishes snacks entertaining  worthy recipes and of course lots of  dessert so for those you who are ready  to ditch the diet and just dive into  delicious naturally nourishing food this  book is really a no-brainer for everyone  on your holiday list so thank you to  everybody who pre-ordered their book if  you haven't already gotten your copy  you're definitely gonna want to purchase  it today you can go on indigo or Amazon  or of course check it out in your local  book store and as soon as you get yours  please leave me a review I would love to  hear what recipes you're enjoying the  most now today I want to share with you  one of my favorite recipes from the book  this is my beet celery a canned brussel  sprout holiday hash it is so delicious  it's great for entertaining this holiday  season because it's gluten free and it's  vegetarian  and it is packed with holiday cheer so  let's do this  [Music]  to a cast-iron skillet I add some olive  oil over medium heat then add in some  onions and garlic and I give it a good  stir  next I add cooked celery AK and cooked  beets and give that a good stir  next I add some shredded Brussels  sprouts beet greens  lemon zest and lemon juice and I stir it  until those greens wilt down finish it  off with some thyme leaves and set it  aside to make my poached eggs I add a  little bit of vinegar to some simmering  water and then I add in my egg now it's  time to assemble top the hash with our  eggs along with some ground pepper  crushed pistachios goats cheese and some  fresh thyme enjoy  [Music]  so guys I hope you enjoyed this recipe  if you did I don't know what you're  waiting for but definitely please pick  up your own copy of the mindful blow  cookbook I worked so incredibly hard on  this baby and I'm so excited to share  with all of you so please leave me a  comment below with what recipes you guys  are loving I also want to see your  photos on Instagram or Twitter or  Facebook so do not forget to tag me  thank you guys so much for watching and  I'll see you next time on Abby's kitchen  bye  [Music]
 

